    "MODERATE: Compute budget violates the ≤200H H100 hard constraint. Inference-only estimate is 170–190h H100, plus fine-tuning (8h A100 × 8 benchmarks = 64h A100 = 32h H100) yields a total of 202–222h H100. The lower bound (202h) already exceeds 200H by 1%, and the upper bound exceeds it by 11%. The proposal's claim that 'the full study fits within the 200H H100 constraint' is arithmetically false. Fix: (a) share fine-tuned checkpoints across related benchmarks (e.g., ACE05 NER and RE share one model; TACRED and TACREV share one; Few-NERD and SciERC could share if schema overlap allows), reducing fine-tuning from ~32h to ~20h H100; or (b) reduce K from 32 to 16 for secondary benchmarks, cutting inference hours ~10–15h H100; either approach brings the total under 200H.",
